#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:9
msgid "Many Particle Model (MPM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:20
msgid ""
"The Many Paticle Model (MPM) of a lithium-ion battery is an extension of the "
"Single Particle Model to account for a continuous distribution of active "
"particle sizes in each electrode :math:`\\text{k}=\\text{n},\\text{p}`. "
"Therefore, many of the same model assumptions hold, e.g., the transport in "
"the electrolyte is instantaneous and hence the through-cell variation (in :"
"math:`x`) is neglected. The full set of assumptions and description of the "
"particle size geometry is given in `[4] <#References>`__. Note that the MPM "
"in `[4] <#References>`__ is for a half cell and the version implemented in "
"PyBaMM is for a full cell and uses the notation and scaling given in `[5] "
"<#References>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:24
msgid "Particle size geometry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:26
msgid ""
"In each electrode :math:`\\text{k}=\\text{n},\\text{p}`, there are spherical "
"particles of each radius :math:`R_\\text{k}` in the range :math:`R_\\text{k,"
"min}<R_\\text{k}<R_\\text{k,max}`, with the fraction of all particles of a "
"given radius :math:`R_\\text{k}` given by the particle-size distribution "
"(base on number) :math:`f_\\text{k,num}(R_\\text{k})`. However, it is more "
"convenient to deal with the fraction of *surface area* contributed by "
"particles of radius :math:`R_\\text{k}`, which we denote :math:`f_{\\text{k},"
"a}(R_\\text{k})` and refer to as the *area-weighted* particle-size "
"distribution. The area and number-based distributions are related via"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:29
msgid ""
"f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k}) = \\frac{4\\pi R_\\text{k}^2 f_\\text{k,num}"
"(R_\\text{k})}{\\int_{R_\\text{k,min}}^{R_\\text{k,max}} 4\\pi R_\\text{k}^2 "
"f_\\text{k,num}(R_\\text{k})\\,\\text{d}R_\\text{k}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:34
msgid ""
"The total amount of surface area (per unit volume) :math:`a_\\text{k,tot}` "
"accounting for all particles is expressed in terms of the active material "
"volume fraction :math:`\\epsilon_{s,\\text{k}}`, similar to the other models "
"in PyBaMM (SPM, DFN):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:36
msgid ""
"\\epsilon_{s,\\text{k}}= \\int \\frac{1}{3} R_\\text{k} "
"\\underbrace{a_\\text{k,tot}f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k})}_{\\text{area }"
"a_\\text{k}(R_\\text{k})\\text{ of particles size }R_\\text{k}}\\,\\text{d}"
"R_\\text{k}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:41
msgid ""
"Rearranging and defining :math:`\\bar{R}_{\\text{k},a}=\\int  R_\\text{k} "
"f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k})\\,\\text{d}R_\\text{k}` as the mean of the area-"
"weighted distribution, we find"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:43
msgid ""
"a_\\text{k,tot}=\\frac{3\\epsilon_{s,\\text{k}}}{\\int  R_\\text{k} "
"f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k})\\,\\text{d}R_\\text{k}} = \\frac{3\\epsilon_{s,"
"\\text{k}}}{\\bar{R}_{\\text{k},a}}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:48
msgid ""
"Then :math:`a_\\text{k,tot}` is the aggregate surface area of the particle "
"population and analogous to the variables ``\"X-averaged negative electrode "
"surface area to volume ratio [m-1]\"``, etc. in the SPM, SPMe, and DFN "
"models, and can be calculated in a similar way as shown above using the "
"*area-weighted mean radius* :math:`\\bar{R}_{\\text{k},a}` (other mean radii "
"do not have this property). See `[4] <#References>`__ for more details on "
"the different types of distribution and mean radii."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:50
msgid ""
"Another common way to express the size distribution is via particle volume. "
"The fraction of volume contributed by the particles of radius :math:"
"`R_\\text{k}`, denoted the *volume-weighted* particle-size distribution is "
"related to the number and area ones via"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:52
msgid ""
"f_{\\text{k},v}(R_\\text{k}) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3} R_\\text{k} f_{\\text{k},"
"a}(R_\\text{k})}{\\int_{R_\\text{k,min}}^{R_\\text{k,max}} \\frac{1}{3} "
"R_\\text{k} f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k})\\,\\text{d}R_\\text{k}} "
"=\\frac{\\frac{4}{3}\\pi R_\\text{k}^3 f_\\text{k,num}(R_\\text{k})}"
"{\\int_{R_\\text{k,min}}^{R_\\text{k,max}} \\frac{4}{3}\\pi R_\\text{k}^3 "
"f_\\text{k,num}(R_\\text{k})\\,\\text{d}R_\\text{k}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:57
msgid ""
"It is sufficient to specify :math:`f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k})`, which is "
"present requirement in the MPM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:69
msgid "Model equations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:71
msgid ""
"In each electrode, only one representative particle of each size :math:"
"`R_\\text{k}` needs to be modelled. The concentration of lithium in the "
"solid particles is denoted :math:`c_{\\text{s,k}}(t,R_\\text{k}, "
"r_\\text{k})`, which varies with time, particle radius :math:`R_\\text{k}`, "
"and the radial coordinate :math:`r_{\\text{k}} \\in[0,R_{\\text{k}}]` within "
"the spherical particle. The potential is uniform across all particles in the "
"electrode, :math:`\\phi_{\\text{s,k}}(t)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:73
msgid ""
"The equations for molar conservation of lithium (:math:`c_{\\text{s,k}}`) "
"are then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:75
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial t} = -\\frac{1}{r_{\\text{k}}^2} "
"\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}} \\left(r_{\\text{k}}^2 "
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\right), \\\\\n"
"N_{\\text{s,k}} = -D_{\\text{s,k}}(c_{\\text{s,k}}) \\frac{\\partial "
"c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:81
msgid ""
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=0} = 0,  \\ \\  N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|"
"_{r_{\\text{k}}=R_{\\text{k}}} =\n"
"\\frac{j_{\\text{k}}}{F} \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p}, \\quad\\\\\n"
"c_{\\text{s,k}}(0,R_\\text{k},r_{\\text{k}}) = c_{\\text{s,k,0}}, \\quad "
"\\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:88
msgid ""
"where :math:`D_{\\text{s,k}}` is the diffusion coefficient in the solid, :"
"math:`N_{\\text{s,k}}` denotes the flux of lithium ions in the solid "
"particle, :math:`F` is Faraday's constant. The interfacial current density "
"is given by :math:`j_\\text{k}`, which also varies with particle size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:91
msgid "Algebraic equations for the potentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:93
msgid ""
"The potentials :math:`\\phi_{\\text{s,k}}(t)` are determined via the "
"integral constraint that the total current flowing across the electrode "
"interface must equal (up to a minus sign) the through-cell current density :"
"math:`i`. Writing this in terms of the potential differences :math:`\\Delta "
"\\phi_{\\text{s,k}} = \\phi_{\\text{s,k}} - \\phi_{\\text{e}}`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:95
msgid ""
"L_\\text{k}a_\\text{k,tot}\\int_{R_\\text{k,min}}^{R_\\text{k,max}} "
"f_{\\text{k},a}(R_\\text{k})j_\\text{k}\\,\\text{d}R_\\text{k} = "
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"i,\\quad \\text{k}=\\text{n}\\\\\n"
"-i,\\quad \\text{k}=\\text{p}\n"
"\\end{cases}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:103
msgid "with Butler-Volmer kinetics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:105
msgid ""
"j_\\text{k}=j_{\\text{0,k}} \\sinh\\left[\\frac{F}{2R_g T}(\\Delta "
"\\phi_{\\text{s,k}}-U_{\\text{k}}(c_{\\text{s},\\text{k}}))\\right], \\ \\ "
"j_{\\text{0,k}} =  m_{\\text{k}}(c_{\\text{e}}c_{\\text{s,k}})^{1/2}"
"(c_\\text{k,max}-c_{\\text{s,k}})^{1/2}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:110
msgid ""
"This gives an integral (or algebraic once discretized) equation for :math:"
"`\\Delta \\phi_{\\text{s,k}}` which is coupled to the concentration "
"equations above. The voltage is then obtained from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/MPM.ipynb:112
msgid "V = \\Delta \\phi_{\\text{s,p}} - \\Delta \\phi_{\\text{s,n}}"
msgstr ""

